// Code signing for the ReadRead target.
//
// The default is ad-hoc ("Sign to Run Locally") on both platforms, so a fresh clone builds with no
// Apple account at all. Ad-hoc still applies the sandbox and network entitlements, and the iOS
// Simulator needs no signing at all, so local behaviour on both platforms is faithful.
//
// Automatic signing wants a "Mac Development" certificate for macOS, which the available
// "Apple Development" identity does not satisfy, and `CODE_SIGN_STYLE` does not reliably honour
// `[sdk=…]` conditionals — so a per-platform split of the *style* does not work.
//
// These live here rather than in `project.yml` so that `Signing.local.xcconfig`, which is
// gitignored, can override them and survive `make generate`. A setting written into the project
// itself would outrank this file, so `project.yml` must not set any of them.
//
// The release workflow passes its own values on the command line, which outrank both files.

CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER =

// Optional: absent in a fresh clone and in CI. See `Signing.local.xcconfig.example`.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
